      "refs": ["D1:L114-L119"]
    },
    {
      "id": "O2",
      "claim": "Observed: the outer record walk advances by 0x30 and processes only records whose first byte is '\\n'; non-'\\n' records are skipped without collection or output.",
      "refs": ["D1:L176-L184","D1:L499-L518"]
    },
    {
      "id": "O3",
      "claim": "Observed: two distinct lookups exist: FUN_140a1c930(uVar6, cmd+4) produces puVar31 payload, while FUN_1405b0ed0(plVar24,&uStack_a0) probes a table and produces separate uStack_a0/uStack_fd fields.",
      "refs": ["D1:L196-L205","D1:L218-L280","D1:L313-L324"]
    },
    {
      "id": "O4",
      "claim": "Inferred: collected indices are reversed in place, then used high-to-low so each tail memmove preserves lower unprocessed indices.",
      "refs": ["D1:L521-L565","D1:L567-L601"]
    }
  ],
